  "description": "Ad-hoc error exploration across all container logs (VictoriaLogs). Built on the log_level field fluentbit's enrich.lua sets. COVERAGE CAVEAT: enrich.lua only extracts BRACKETED levels ([Error]/[ERR]/[error]). Services that don't bracket their logs — VictoriaMetrics, VictoriaLogs, fluentbit itself, cadvisor — emit no log_level, so their errors are NOT counted here. Those log to journald and the ones that matter are watched by vmalert directly. PRIVACY: the 'Recent error lines' table shows raw log content, which may include file paths / URLs / tokens from services like qBittorrent — acceptable here because Grafana is LAN-only (UFW) behind login auth.",
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "barchart",
      "title": "Top error producers (24h)",
      "gridPos": {"h": 10, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 0},
      "datasource": {"type": "victoriametrics-logs-datasource", "uid": "victorialogs"},
      "targets": [{"refId": "A", "datasource": {"type": "victoriametrics-logs-datasource", "uid": "victorialogs"}, "expr": "log_level:error AND _time:24h | stats by (container_name) count() as errors | sort by (errors desc) | limit 20", "queryType": "stats"}],
      "options": {"orientation": "horizontal", "showValue": "auto", "stacking": "none", "legend": {"showLegend": false, "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom"}, "tooltip": {"mode": "single", "sort": "none"}, "xTickLabelRotation": 0},
      "fieldConfig": {"defaults": {"color": {"mode": "palette-classic"}, "custom": {"fillOpacity": 80, "lineWidth": 1}}, "overrides": []}
    },
    {
